  "question_quotes": [
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-01",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 1,
      "passage_id": "cbti_analysis",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/body[1]/sec[2]/sec[6]/p[1]",
        "start": 424,
        "end": 486,
        "quote": "Analyses were conducted based on the intent-to-treat approach."
      }
    },
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-01",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 2,
      "passage_id": "cbti_primary",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/body[1]/sec[3]/sec[2]/p[1]",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 219,
        "quote": "Thirty-seven participants (incidence proportion, 10%; 37/354) in the intervention group and 62 participants (incidence proportion, 18%; 62/354) in the control group developed new-onset MDD during the 12-month follow-up."
      }
    },
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-01",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 3,
      "passage_id": "cbti_primary",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/body[1]/sec[3]/sec[2]/p[1]",
        "start": 568,
        "end": 675,
        "quote": "Cox regression revealed an HR of 0.58 (0.38–0.87; p = 0.008) for MDD favoring app-based CBT-I intervention."
      }
    },
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-01",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 4,
      "passage_id": "cbti_abstract",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/front[1]/article-meta[1]/abstract[1]/sec[2]/p[1]",
        "start": 634,
        "end": 1035,
        "quote": "708 participants (407 females [57%]; mean age, 22.1 years [SD = 1.9]) were randomly allocated to app-based CBT-I group (n = 354) or app-based HE group (n = 354). Thirty-seven participants (10%) in the intervention group and 62 participants (18%) in the control group developed new-onset MDD throughout the 12-month follow-up, with a hazard ratio of 0.58 (95% confidence interval 0.38–0.87; p = 0.008)."
      }
    },
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-01",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 5,
      "passage_id": "cbti_exploratory",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/body[1]/sec[3]/sec[2]/p[2]",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 347,
        "quote": "After additionally adjusting for prior history of MDD, educational level, family income, comorbid medical illnesses, and use of sleep-promoting medications in exploratory analysis, the risk of developing MDD remained significantly lower for the app-based CBT-I intervention group compared with the controls (adjusted HR 0.60 [0.40–0.90]; p = 0.01)"
      }
    },
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-02",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 1,
      "passage_id": "cbti_remission_definition",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/body[1]/sec[2]/sec[4]/p[2]",
        "start": 118,
        "end": 406,
        "quote": "Remission of insomnia disorder was determined by the following criteria [21]: (1) no functional impairments or distress with sleep, (2) insomnia symptoms less than three times per week for at least 1 month, and (3) sleep-promoting medication use less than once per week in the past month."
      }
    },
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-02",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 2,
      "passage_id": "cbti_remission_results",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/body[1]/sec[3]/sec[3]/sec[1]/p[1]",
        "start": 113,
        "end": 429,
        "quote": "At post-intervention, the weighted percentage of remitters based on clinical interviews in app-based CBT-I group was higher than that of the app-based HE group (52% versus 28%; relative risk [RR] 1.83 [95% CI 1.49–2.24]; p < 0.001) after controlling for strata variables and accounting for the missing data patterns."
      }
    },
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-02",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 3,
      "passage_id": "cbti_analysis",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/body[1]/sec[2]/sec[6]/p[1]",
        "start": 695,
        "end": 952,
        "quote": "Remission rates of insomnia were analyzed using a weighted generalized estimating equations model. Weights were computed as the product of a missing model weight to attenuate the effect of attrition conditional on strata variables and group allocation [32]."
      }
    },
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-02",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 4,
      "passage_id": "cbti_analysis",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/body[1]/sec[2]/sec[6]/p[1]",
        "start": 1799,
        "end": 1872,
        "quote": "Strata variables at baseline were included as covariates in all analyses."
      }
    },
    {
      "question_id": "v3-cbti-02",
      "split": "held-out",
      "span_ordinal": 5,
      "passage_id": "cbti_abstract",
      "article_alias": "cbti",
      "anchor": {
        "block_id": "xml:/article[1]/front[1]/article-meta[1]/abstract[1]/sec[2]/p[1]",
        "start": 1109,
        "end": 1281,
        "quote": "The app-based CBT-I group has higher remission rates of insomnia disorder than the controls at post-intervention (52% versus 28%; relative risk 1.83 [1.49–2.24]; p < 0.001)"
      }
    },
    {
